        "Mobile networks in the real world do not behave like the diagrams. A customer taps to pay, the money leaves their wallet, and then the operator's confirmation SMS takes thirty seconds, a minute, sometimes two or three to actually arrive. A naive verification system, seeing no confirmation in the instant it checks, has already failed the sale and moved on — leaving a paying customer standing there insisting they sent the money. {{brand}} is built for that real network, not the ideal one, which is why late payment verification is a core behaviour rather than an afterthought.",
