      body: [
        "{{brand}}'s partner programme is for people who want to earn from mobile money verification rather than only use it. It comes in two roles. A reseller buys verification inventory — account credit, called ACU, or signed voucher PINs — at 80% of the list price, and resells it at list, keeping the 20% spread. A distributor buys float at 85% and keeps 15%, trading a slightly thinner margin for larger volume and standing credit. In both cases you are selling the one thing the whole platform runs on: the ability to confirm, in about three seconds, that a mobile money payment is genuinely real. The full partner terms live on {{page:rails}}.",
        "What makes this a comfortable business to run is that it is entirely prepaid. You buy your inventory up front, so there is no credit to chase and — crucially — no chargebacks to fear. A reseller of card-based products lives with the constant risk that a sale is reversed weeks later; here the money you take for a voucher or a float top-up is final the moment the merchant pays you. You are never out of pocket for a sale that unwinds, and you carry no perishable stock: ACU does not expire on a shelf, and a voucher PIN simply waits until it is redeemed.",
        "The economics are deliberately simple. Every $100 of voucher inventory bought at the 80% wholesale rate resells for $125, so you keep $25. Every $100 of float bought at the 85% distributor rate resells for about $117.65, leaving you $17.65. Scale it and the spread compounds: a reseller moving $1,000 of inventory a week keeps roughly $200 a week, with no inventory risk and nothing to reconcile against a bank. The live figures and current wholesale rates are always shown on {{page:rails}}.",
        "You do not need to be technical, and you do not need any special device. Partners sell the way their customers already buy — face to face at a kiosk, over SMS, or with printed PINs handed across a counter like scratch cards. A cyber café, an airtime dealer, a mobile money agent or a neighbourhood shop can add {{brand}} to what they already sell without changing anything about how they operate. The signed voucher system that makes this possible, including how PINs are redeemed completely offline, is explained in {{post:mobile-money-vouchers-pins-offline}}.",
        "Operationally the loop is short. You top up your partner balance, draw down either ACU float or a batch of signed voucher PINs, and sell them on to merchants in your area. A merchant redeems a PIN or receives float, and it converts straight into verification credit — or a 30-day plan — on their own {{brand}} account. Because merchants who can pay {{brand}} directly get the lower direct price, the list price you sell at is simply the convenience premium a cash customer happily pays for being served locally, in person, today.",
        "It is worth being clear about how this differs from referring merchants, because {{brand}} runs both and they reward different things. The partner programme pays you a wholesale margin on inventory you buy and resell — you are a merchant of {{brand}} credit. The referral programme, described in {{post:refer-merchants-earn-credit}}, instead pays a lifetime commission on merchants you introduce who then pay {{brand}} directly. Many partners do both: they resell inventory for immediate margin and refer the larger merchants who would rather hold their own account, earning on both sides of the same relationship.",
        "Every merchant you bring onto {{brand}}, whether by selling them inventory or referring them, becomes part of a network that grows more valuable as it grows — the shared fraud defence in {{post:shared-fraud-network}} protects all of them at once, which makes the product easier to keep selling. If you want a prepaid, chargeback-free line of business with margins you can see and scale at your own pace, this is it. Read the terms and current rates on {{page:rails}}, see how partners fit the wider growth engine on {{page:growth}}, and when you are ready, {{page:getstarted}}.",
      ],
